    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0168" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg72"/>

                <head>No. 48.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr. Partridge.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 21,
                        1871</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 19.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your dispatch No. 13, of the
                    23d ultimo, communicating the agreeable intelligence of the appointment by the
                    princess regent of Brazil, in the name of the Emperor, of Baron de Itajubá to be
                    a member of the Tribunal of Arbitration under Article of the <pb facs="0169"
                        n="73" xml:id="pg73"/> Treaty of Washington, I have to express to you the
                    sincere gratification afforded to the President by the selection of so eminent
                    and learned a gentleman.</p>
                <p>I am. &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. C. B. DAVIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
